 "document": {
  "id": "D08",
  "path": "conversations/conv_pines023_patron_characteristics.eml",
  "text": "From: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org\nTo: pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Patron reports by demographics - how?\nDate: Wed, 29 Apr 2009 09:15:00 -0500\n\nI need to run reports on patrons grouped by characteristics. The fields\nI need:\n- Age range\n- Zip code\n- County of residence\n- Home branch\n- Patron type\n- Preferred language\n\nIs this possible?\n\nMaria\nP.S. Does anyone else's cat sit on their keyboard when you're trying to\nwork? Mine does it on purpose, I'm convinced.\n===\nFrom: jennifer.durham@statesboro.lib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Patron reports by demographics - how?\nDate: Wed, 29 Apr 2009 09:50:00 -0500\n\nYes, this is essential! We use these reports for program planning. Last\nmonth we targeted a summer reading program for teenagers, so we ran a\nreport on patrons aged 13-18 in our zip code.\n\nCan we also GROUP BY these fields? Like, show me circulation by age range,\nor patron count by home branch?\n\nMy son has his science fair project due next week. He's building a volcano\nthat erupts with baking soda and vinegar. Classic.\n\n-Jenny\n===\nFrom: susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, jennifer.durham@statesboro.lib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Patron reports by demographics - how?\nDate: Wed, 29 Apr 2009 10:30:00 -0500\n\nI need to be able to both LIMIT and GROUP BY patron characteristics.\nFor example:\n- Limit: Show me only patrons in zip code 30501\n- Group By: Show me checkout counts grouped by age range\n\nThe age ranges need to be configurable too. Like, 0-5, 6-10, 11-15, etc.\nOr 0-6, 7-12, 13-17, 18-24, 25-34... Whatever makes sense for the report.\n\nGot my haircut yesterday. Finally got rid of that awkward growing-out phase.\nFeels so much better.\n===\nFrom: latoya.davidson@twinlakeslib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, jennifer.durham@statesboro.lib.org, susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Patron reports by demographics - how?\nDate: Wed, 29 Apr 2009 11:15:00 -0500\n\nPreferred language is interesting - we have patrons who prefer Spanish,\nVietnamese, Korean, and various other languages. This helps us decide which\nmaterials to purchase in translation.\n\nAlso, \"patron type\" is important - adult, juvenile, senior, student, etc.\nDifferent types have different borrowing privileges.\n\nCan we combine demographic filters? Like \"show me all Juvenile patrons in\nzip code 30505 who haven't checked anything out in 6 months\"?\n\nMy mom just asked me to help her set up FaceTime on her new iPhone. She's\n72 and technology is... an adventure.\n===\nFrom: dana.peeler@ohoopeelib.org\nTo: maria.rodriguez@dalton-whitman.lib.org, jennifer.durham@statesboro.lib.org, susansexton-cooley@saraboblib.org, latoya.davidson@twinlakeslib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Patron reports by demographics - how?\nDate: Wed, 29 Apr 2009 12:00:00 -0500\n\nI think we should also consider what data is available. Some of these\nfields might not be consistently populated. For example, not all patrons\nprovide their zip code or county.\n\nShould the report show nulls for missing data, or exclude those records?\n\nI spilled coffee on my shirt this morning. It's going to be one of those days.\n===\nFrom: robert.chen@gapubliclib.org\nTo: dana.peeler@ohoopeelib.org, pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: Re: Patron reports by demographics - how?\nDate: Wed, 29 Apr 2009 13:45:00 -0500\n\nFrom a technical standpoint, these queries are straightforward. All the\nfields mentioned (age range, zip code, county, home branch, patron type,\npreferred language) exist in the patron table.\n\nThe \"age range\" is calculated from the birth_date field, which means we\nneed to compute it at query time. We can create age brackets in the query.\n\nCombining filters is also doable - just add WHERE clauses. We can support\nboth AND and OR logic.\n\nOne consideration: if patrons haven't provided optional fields, they'll\nshow up as null. We should include them in the report (with null values)\nrather than excluding them, because excluding data silently can lead to\nmisleading results.\n\nMy new monitor arrived today. Dual screens, here I come!\n===\nFrom: katherine.gregory@gapubliclib.org\nTo: pines-reports-working-group@gapl.org\nSubject: SUMMARY: Patron characteristics requirement\nDate: Thu, 30 Apr 2009 09:00:00 -0500\n\nRequirement consolidated:\n\nThe system should allow queries and reports to be limited or grouped by\nvarious patron characteristics, including:\n- Age range\n- Zip code\n- County of residence\n- Home branch\n- Patron type\n- Preferred language\n\nKey points:\n- Both LIMIT (filter) and GROUP BY (aggregate) should be supported\n- Filters can be combined with AND/OR logic\n- Null values should be included in results\n- Age ranges should be configurable per report\n\nAction: Robert confirmed technical feasibility. Jenny will provide test cases\nfrom her summer reading program planning.\n\n-Katherine\n(P.S. Maria - yes, cats sit on keyboards on purpose. It's a universal law.)"
 },
 "requirements": [
